NICE(2)                        P32W Unix                         NICE(2)

NAME
       nice - change the scheduling priority (does nothing)

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int nice(int incr);

DESCRIPTION
       In V7, nice lowers (or, for the super-user, raises) the
       priority of the calling process. P32W's scheduler is plain
       round-robin with no priorities: nice accepts any incr, does
       nothing, and returns 0.

RETURN VALUE
       0.

SEE ALSO
       fork(2), ps(1)

BUGS
       It exists only so that old programs link and run.
